WEBVTT

1
00:00:48.771 --> 00:00:50.637
<i>Who are we?</i>

2
00:00:50.731 --> 00:00:54.315
<i>Are we simply what others
want us to be?</i>

3
00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:58.441
<i>Are we destined to a fate
beyond our control?</i>

4
00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:01.740
<i>Or can we evolve?</i>

5
00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:06.115
<i>Become... something more?</i>

6
00:01:12.628 --> 00:01:13.994
Can you change the station?

7
00:01:14.088 --> 00:01:16.330
When the song's over, honey.

8
00:01:16.422 --> 00:01:19.166
You said that two songs ago.

9
00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:21.797
You know this is
a classic, right?

10
00:01:21.887 --> 00:01:24.095
Okay, how about
I make you a promise?

11
00:01:24.181 --> 00:01:26.092
When you're old enough
to drive,

12
00:01:26.183 --> 00:01:28.970
you can listen to whatever
music you want. Hmm?

13
00:01:29.061 --> 00:01:31.223
That a deal?

14
00:01:34.565 --> 00:01:36.979
- John.
- Wasn't me.

15
00:01:37.945 --> 00:01:40.152
Jean, was that... Did you?

16
00:01:40.238 --> 00:01:42.196
I didn't do anything.

17
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:54.125
- Jean, what are you...
- I... I don't know. It's not me.

18
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.381
Quiet.

19
00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:05.503
Quiet.

20
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.932
Quiet!

21
00:03:15.292 --> 00:03:17.329
She doesn't have a scratch on her.

22
00:03:17.419 --> 00:03:19.251
No internal injuries.

23
00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:23.548
And you're sure she was in the car?

24
00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:24.875
Yeah.

25
00:03:25.761 --> 00:03:27.548
Who's gonna tell her?

26
00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.466
Thank you.

27
00:03:37.314 --> 00:03:38.350
Hello.

28
00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.272
Where are my parents?

29
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.731
My name's
Charles Xavier, and...

30
00:03:44.822 --> 00:03:46.529
They're dead.

31
00:03:46.615 --> 00:03:47.947
Aren't they?

32
00:03:51.954 --> 00:03:53.570
Yes, they are.

33
00:03:53.664 --> 00:03:57.283
And I'm very sorry
to have to tell you that.

34
00:04:00.629 --> 00:04:02.586
So what happens to me now?

35
00:04:06.385 --> 00:04:07.921
Well, that's why I'm here, actually.

36
00:04:08.887 --> 00:04:10.298
You see, I have a school

37
00:04:10.389 --> 00:04:13.723
that is for young people,
who are like you.

38
00:04:13.809 --> 00:04:15.016
Special.

39
00:04:15.102 --> 00:04:17.388
Special is just
a nice word for...

40
00:04:17.478 --> 00:04:20.392
Weird? Or crazy?

41
00:04:20.481 --> 00:04:22.017
Yep.

42
00:04:22.108 --> 00:04:24.101
Yep, sometimes it is.

43
00:04:24.986 --> 00:04:26.068
Ooh.

44
00:04:26.154 --> 00:04:28.316
Sometimes, it can be a word

45
00:04:28.407 --> 00:04:30.524
used to describe people
who are significant.

46
00:04:30.616 --> 00:04:32.448
Or amazing. Or...

47
00:04:32.536 --> 00:04:35.495
Or just... just really cool.

48
00:04:37.707 --> 00:04:39.620
You've got gifts, Jean.

49
00:04:43.046 --> 00:04:44.537
Do you know what?

50
00:04:46.842 --> 00:04:49.003
Take this pen, right.

51
00:04:49.844 --> 00:04:51.801
It's something that...

52
00:04:51.888 --> 00:04:55.007
Well, actually, just take it.

53
00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:56.556
It's a gift.

54
00:05:00.606 --> 00:05:02.938
Now, you could choose to draw

55
00:05:03.025 --> 00:05:04.857
a really good picture
with that...

56
00:05:04.943 --> 00:05:09.688
or you could use it
to poke someone's eyes out.

57
00:05:09.781 --> 00:05:13.070
But either way,
it's still just a pen.

58
00:05:13.159 --> 00:05:15.868
It's just a gift.

59
00:05:15.954 --> 00:05:18.320
And what you choose
to do with your gift,

60
00:05:18.414 --> 00:05:20.998
well, that's
entirely up to you.

61
00:05:22.376 --> 00:05:25.039
But if you want to use it
to do good stuff...

62
00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:28.544
well, I can help.

63
00:05:29.676 --> 00:05:31.962
You're not like
the other doctors.

64
00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.926
No.

65
00:05:36.808 --> 00:05:39.015
And you're not like
the other patients.

66
00:06:06.212 --> 00:06:07.829
What do you think?

67
00:06:10.424 --> 00:06:11.882
I can't stay here.

68
00:06:13.719 --> 00:06:15.676
Okay. Why not?

69
00:06:15.763 --> 00:06:17.505
It's too nice.

70
00:06:18.265 --> 00:06:20.132
I...

71
00:06:21.602 --> 00:06:24.436
- I break things.
- Well, how does this sound:

72
00:06:24.522 --> 00:06:27.732
If you break something,
anything, I can fix it.

73
00:06:27.818 --> 00:06:29.525
Not anything.

74
00:06:30.404 --> 00:06:31.986
I can help you.

75
00:06:33.532 --> 00:06:36.092
I can help you so that you never
have to break things ever again.

76
00:06:37.327 --> 00:06:38.909
You think you can fix me too.

77
00:06:39.454 --> 00:06:40.786
No.

78
00:06:44.626 --> 00:06:49.121
No, because
you are not broken.

79
00:07:05.313 --> 00:07:08.772
<i>Ten, nine, eight, seven,</i>

80
00:07:08.859 --> 00:07:14.856
<i>six, five, four,
three, two, one...</i>

81
00:07:38.847 --> 00:07:39.948
<i>Engines throttling up.</i>

82
00:07:39.972 --> 00:07:41.680
<i>Three engines now at 104%.</i>

83
00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.769
Hey, I'm...
I'm picking something up here.

84
00:07:47.856 --> 00:07:50.563
Ma'am, I've got something
on sat six.

85
00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.570
<i>Houston, we have a problem.</i>

86
00:07:59.284 --> 00:08:01.804
<i>Space Shuttle</i> Endeavour
<i>has encountered problems on its mission.</i>

87
00:08:01.828 --> 00:08:03.638
- I know what you're thinking.
- That's my trick.

88
00:08:03.662 --> 00:08:05.515
And the answer is no.
The jet can't get that high.

89
00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:08.157
Even with the new booster rockets
and all your modifications?

90
00:08:08.251 --> 00:08:10.709
They're built for acceleration,
not elevation, okay?

91
00:08:10.796 --> 00:08:13.664
Not this. No.

92
00:08:13.757 --> 00:08:15.525
<i>They've lost thrust vector control.</i>

93
00:08:15.549 --> 00:08:17.837
<i>Trajectory settings are irregular,</i>

94
00:08:17.928 --> 00:08:20.010
<i>likely from the constant engine burn.</i>

95
00:08:20.597 --> 00:08:22.805
<i>Oxygen generation is down...</i>

96
00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.053
Yes? Yes, this is he.

97
00:08:26.977 --> 00:08:29.469
- Charles?
- Mr. President.

98
00:08:29.563 --> 00:08:31.351
Are you seeing this on TV?

99
00:08:31.441 --> 00:08:33.023
Yes, I'm watching now.

100
00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.351
Hank?

101
00:08:38.365 --> 00:08:39.400
Yeah.

102
00:08:45.329 --> 00:08:46.662
It's a simple extraction.

103
00:08:46.747 --> 00:08:47.954
We go into space,

104
00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:49.828
we get the astronauts,
we bring them home.

105
00:08:49.918 --> 00:08:52.456
- Any questions?
- Yeah, like a thousand.

106
00:08:52.545 --> 00:08:53.912
We don't have time
for a thousand.

107
00:08:54.005 --> 00:08:55.121
So we're going to space?

108
00:08:55.215 --> 00:08:57.207
Yes, Kurt,
we are going into space.

109
00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.792
We're doing space
missions now. Cool.

110
00:08:59.886 --> 00:09:01.343
Will the X-Jet
even get that high?

111
00:09:01.429 --> 00:09:03.887
- Well, technically, the...
- It will get us there.

112
00:09:03.973 --> 00:09:05.385
Let's go.

113
00:09:09.938 --> 00:09:11.429
Are you okay with this?

114
00:09:11.523 --> 00:09:13.936
I forget sometimes
you can read minds.

115
00:09:14.025 --> 00:09:15.436
I didn't need
to read your mind.

116
00:09:15.526 --> 00:09:17.860
It's written all over your face.

117
00:09:17.946 --> 00:09:20.858
You tell me it's good,
it's good.

118
00:09:20.949 --> 00:09:23.111
If anything goes wrong,

119
00:09:23.201 --> 00:09:24.817
I'll turn us around
in a heartbeat.

120
00:09:25.954 --> 00:09:27.661
I know you will.

121
00:09:52.981 --> 00:09:55.223
<i>A second ship has been spotted in the sky.</i>

122
00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.963
<i>We are being told the president</i>

123
00:09:58.987 --> 00:10:01.730
<i>has called in the aid
of the X-Men.</i>

124
00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:31.763
Ladies and gentlemen of NASA,
this is the voice of Charles Xavier.

125
00:10:31.853 --> 00:10:33.970
Could somebody please
apprise me of the situation?

126
00:10:34.064 --> 00:10:36.146
We were picking up
solar flares.

127
00:10:36.233 --> 00:10:38.646
We believe the heat
shorted out their electricity.

128
00:10:38.735 --> 00:10:41.021
<i>They lost control,
communication, orientation,</i>

129
00:10:41.112 --> 00:10:42.694
<i>pretty much everything.</i>

130
00:10:42.781 --> 00:10:45.148
Not to worry, Mission Control.
Help is on the way.

131
00:10:57.212 --> 00:11:00.626
I think this is not as much
fun as I thought it would be.

132
00:11:29.119 --> 00:11:31.281
That's a solar flare?

133
00:11:31.371 --> 00:11:33.658
I've never seen
a reading like this.

134
00:11:53.893 --> 00:11:56.385
The orientation thruster's misfiring.

135
00:11:56.478 --> 00:11:59.347
- That cabin won't hold for long.
- Kurt, can you get in there?

136
00:11:59.441 --> 00:12:02.058
It's spinning too fast.
I can't see inside the window.

137
00:12:02.151 --> 00:12:04.269
Scott, I need you
to blast that thruster,

138
00:12:04.362 --> 00:12:05.978
slow down the spin.

139
00:12:25.632 --> 00:12:27.841
Kurt, take Peter. Go!

140
00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:34.932
<i>Storm, seal those cracks.</i>

141
00:12:42.275 --> 00:12:44.187
Be right back.

142
00:12:50.699 --> 00:12:51.906
Oh, shit.

143
00:13:04.798 --> 00:13:06.608
- Strap in, we're headed home.
- Wait.

144
00:13:06.632 --> 00:13:08.499
Our commander, he's not here.

145
00:13:09.177 --> 00:13:11.134
He was in the airlock
working on the thruster.

146
00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:17.262
The heat signature's
rising fast.

147
00:13:17.352 --> 00:13:19.468
I can't hold it any longer.

148
00:13:19.562 --> 00:13:22.225
We gotta get out of here.
I said strap in.

149
00:13:22.314 --> 00:13:24.728
No, Raven. No.
We're not leaving anyone behind.

150
00:13:24.818 --> 00:13:27.151
I am not putting this team
in more danger.

151
00:13:27.237 --> 00:13:29.228
What about their team?

152
00:13:29.322 --> 00:13:30.722
Jean can hold
that shuttle together.

153
00:13:30.781 --> 00:13:32.614
<i>Can't you, Jean?</i>

154
00:13:32.699 --> 00:13:35.864
You know you can do anything
you set your mind to.

155
00:13:35.954 --> 00:13:38.662
I can hold the ship together
but not from here.

156
00:13:38.747 --> 00:13:41.161
- I need to get inside.
- The heat's spiking.

157
00:13:41.251 --> 00:13:43.062
We've got less than a minute
till those flares hit.

158
00:13:43.086 --> 00:13:44.418
She said she can do it.

159
00:13:46.172 --> 00:13:47.413
Thirty seconds.

160
00:13:51.261 --> 00:13:52.877
Count it down. Go.

161
00:14:13.158 --> 00:14:14.819
We got 20 seconds.

162
00:14:24.294 --> 00:14:25.375
Ten...

163
00:14:25.462 --> 00:14:27.454
<i>nine, eight...</i>

164
00:14:27.547 --> 00:14:29.254
<i>seven, six...</i>

165
00:14:30.049 --> 00:14:31.049
<i>five...</i>

166
00:14:31.384 --> 00:14:32.545
four...

167
00:14:32.635 --> 00:14:33.842
three...

168
00:14:33.928 --> 00:14:35.089
<i>two...</i>

169
00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:36.180
one.

170
00:14:43.563 --> 00:14:45.475
Where's Jean?
Kurt, where is she?

171
00:14:45.564 --> 00:14:48.808
- Where is she?
- I'm sorry!

172
00:14:52.572 --> 00:14:53.983
Brace for impact.

173
00:16:38.886 --> 00:16:40.047
Is every...

174
00:16:41.139 --> 00:16:42.630
Is everybody okay?

175
00:16:43.308 --> 00:16:45.800
Yeah, we're okay.

176
00:16:49.271 --> 00:16:51.309
So let's go home.

177
00:17:02.702 --> 00:17:04.443
- Yay, X-Men! Woo!
- Yeah!

178
00:17:09.666 --> 00:17:11.579
Yeah! X-Men!

179
00:17:33.650 --> 00:17:35.937
That's enough,
boys and girls. That's enough.

180
00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:41.029
The X-Men have today done
an incredibly brave thing.

181
00:17:41.115 --> 00:17:43.858
They've once again proved to humanity
exactly why they need us,

182
00:17:43.951 --> 00:17:46.113
people like yourselves.

183
00:17:46.204 --> 00:17:48.036
The president sends his regards,

184
00:17:48.122 --> 00:17:50.158
as well as his
heartfelt gratitude.

185
00:17:50.249 --> 00:17:53.993
And, as for myself,
I've never been prouder.

186
00:17:55.046 --> 00:17:57.959
Enjoy yourselves.
You certainly deserve it.

187
00:17:58.049 --> 00:17:59.256
In fact, you all do.

188
00:17:59.341 --> 00:18:00.708
No more class,
the end of the day.

189
00:18:03.638 --> 00:18:04.638
Jean?

190
00:18:06.557 --> 00:18:09.049
You gave us quite a scare up there.
How are you feeling?

191
00:18:10.228 --> 00:18:12.971
Actually, I... I feel fine.

192
00:18:13.064 --> 00:18:15.101
- Hank?
- Yeah?

193
00:18:15.191 --> 00:18:16.293
Would you take a look at Jean?

194
00:18:16.317 --> 00:18:18.650
Standard medical
for anyone injured in the field.

195
00:18:18.735 --> 00:18:20.102
Thank you.

196
00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:25.074
You know, the president
was almost sending his condolences.

197
00:18:25.158 --> 00:18:28.743
- She should be dead.
- Thankfully, she's not.

198
00:18:31.666 --> 00:18:33.202
I basically did everything.

199
00:18:33.292 --> 00:18:35.658
I mean, Jean did a little,
like towards the end,

200
00:18:35.753 --> 00:18:37.460
but it was mostly all me.

201
00:18:41.591 --> 00:18:43.208
You put us in danger, Charles.

202
00:18:43.302 --> 00:18:46.136
You put those kids in danger.

203
00:18:47.557 --> 00:18:50.391
They're not kids anymore, Raven.

204
00:18:51.602 --> 00:18:54.970
And I care about their safety
just as much as you do.

205
00:18:55.064 --> 00:18:57.226
Are you sure about that?

206
00:18:57.316 --> 00:18:59.899
'Cause we're taking bigger
and bigger risks.

207
00:18:59.985 --> 00:19:01.067
And for what?

208
00:19:01.154 --> 00:19:04.192
Please, tell me it's not your ego.

209
00:19:04.282 --> 00:19:05.989
Being on the cover
of magazines,

210
00:19:06.075 --> 00:19:08.112
getting a medal from the president.

211
00:19:08.202 --> 00:19:09.568
You like it, don't you?

212
00:19:09.662 --> 00:19:11.619
As opposed to being
hunted and despised?

213
00:19:11.706 --> 00:19:13.072
Well, you know, actually, I do.

214
00:19:13.166 --> 00:19:15.249
It's all just a means
to an end, Raven.

215
00:19:15.334 --> 00:19:17.872
- What end is that?
- Keeping us safe.

216
00:19:17.962 --> 00:19:19.356
You should understand
better than anyone

217
00:19:19.379 --> 00:19:21.292
that we're only ever
one bad day away

218
00:19:21.382 --> 00:19:23.624
from them starting to see us
as the enemy again.

219
00:19:23.718 --> 00:19:25.960
So, what?
We wear matching costumes

220
00:19:26.053 --> 00:19:27.531
and smile in pictures
to make everyone feel safe?

221
00:19:27.555 --> 00:19:29.283
That is a small price to pay
for keeping the peace.

222
00:19:29.307 --> 00:19:32.550
- By risking our people to save theirs?
- Yes! Yes!

223
00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.476
It's funny.

224
00:19:38.566 --> 00:19:40.649
I can't actually remember the last time

225
00:19:40.735 --> 00:19:42.192
you were the one risking something.

226
00:19:42.278 --> 00:19:43.735
And by the way,

227
00:19:43.821 --> 00:19:46.234
the women are always saving
the men around here.

228
00:19:46.324 --> 00:19:48.737
You might wanna think about
changing the name to X-Women.

229
00:19:50.953 --> 00:19:53.445
Your heartbeat's strong,
pulse is good,

230
00:19:53.539 --> 00:19:55.405
brain activity is normal.

231
00:19:56.751 --> 00:19:57.751
The genetic reading,

232
00:19:57.835 --> 00:19:59.952
I'm gonna take another look at.

233
00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:04.831
What can't be right?

234
00:20:05.968 --> 00:20:07.613
Did you just read my mind
without permission?

235
00:20:07.637 --> 00:20:11.756
Sorry, I didn't mean to,
but what can't be right?

236
00:20:13.893 --> 00:20:16.977
Whatever happened up there
made you stronger.

237
00:20:18.231 --> 00:20:19.833
You know, I've never seen
a power reading like this.

238
00:20:19.857 --> 00:20:23.146
You're-You're literally...
I mean, you're off the charts.

239
00:20:23.235 --> 00:20:25.478
So what does that mean?

240
00:20:25.571 --> 00:20:27.812
It means, um...

241
00:20:28.491 --> 00:20:31.404
we'll have to build a better machine.

242
00:20:31.494 --> 00:20:34.658
But... how do you feel?

243
00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.157
I feel good.

244
00:20:38.251 --> 00:20:39.492
Good.

245
00:20:39.585 --> 00:20:42.999
Well, as far as I can tell,
you're good to go.

246
00:20:43.089 --> 00:20:45.297
- You can head upstairs.
- All right.

247
00:20:47.593 --> 00:20:49.084
Thanks, Hank.

248
00:20:54.475 --> 00:20:55.841
<i>Hank said that?</i>

249
00:20:55.935 --> 00:20:57.551
- "Off the charts"?
- He did.

250
00:20:57.645 --> 00:20:59.602
The big blue furry guy?
The doctor? That Hank?

251
00:20:59.689 --> 00:21:01.180
That's the one. Why?

252
00:21:03.609 --> 00:21:05.601
You a little intimidated, maybe?

253
00:21:05.695 --> 00:21:07.687
Constantly.

254
00:21:10.199 --> 00:21:11.781
- Jean. Jean...
- Hmm?

255
00:21:13.661 --> 00:21:15.197
Are you...
Are you sure you're okay?

256
00:21:15.955 --> 00:21:19.790
I'm better than okay.
God, I feel great, I do.

257
00:21:20.626 --> 00:21:24.415
I don't know, I feel like
everything is just...

258
00:21:24.504 --> 00:21:26.245
turned up.

259
00:21:27.174 --> 00:21:29.040
Yeah.

260
00:21:29.135 --> 00:21:32.253
- No, it's just...
- Just what?

261
00:21:35.141 --> 00:21:37.258
I thought I lost you today.

262
00:21:37.351 --> 00:21:38.841
I know.

263
00:21:40.521 --> 00:21:42.683
But I came back to you.

264
00:21:43.691 --> 00:21:45.899
I'll always come back to you.

265
00:22:18.142 --> 00:22:19.349
Is that Luna?

266
00:22:20.728 --> 00:22:22.310
Probably just squirrels.

267
00:22:24.023 --> 00:22:26.356
Mm...?

268
00:22:27.568 --> 00:22:29.605
I'm just gonna check on her.
I'll be right back.

269
00:22:29.695 --> 00:22:30.731
Just stay.

270
00:22:33.407 --> 00:22:35.865
- Tell her to shut up.
- Luna!

271
00:22:39.538 --> 00:22:40.745
Luna!

272
00:22:57.139 --> 00:22:58.139
Luna!

273
00:22:59.433 --> 00:23:00.764
Honey!

274
00:23:02.728 --> 00:23:04.936
What is it?
What is it, honey?

275
00:23:34.135 --> 00:23:36.377
He's got the dumbest laugh.

276
00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:37.756
That's not...

277
00:23:38.472 --> 00:23:39.633
That's not how it happened.

278
00:23:39.724 --> 00:23:42.182
- Oh, my God.
- That was...

279
00:23:47.231 --> 00:23:48.642
Margaret?

280
00:23:52.028 --> 00:23:53.064
What...?

281
00:24:30.191 --> 00:24:31.807
- This way.
- Okay.

282
00:24:33.485 --> 00:24:34.567
One more?

283
00:24:34.653 --> 00:24:36.485
Yeah, I'll go ahead
and finish this one.

284
00:24:40.367 --> 00:24:41.653
Two more?

285
00:24:43.245 --> 00:24:44.531
Uh, yeah.

286
00:24:49.585 --> 00:24:51.747
- Hey.
- Rocks.

287
00:24:53.464 --> 00:24:54.796
Thanks.

288
00:24:55.549 --> 00:24:57.836
- How is she doing?
- She's, uh...

289
00:24:59.386 --> 00:25:02.003
- thirsty.
- Yeah, I see that.

290
00:25:02.098 --> 00:25:03.930
Does she seem okay to you?

291
00:25:04.016 --> 00:25:06.929
For someone who's just been
hit with solar flares...

292
00:25:07.019 --> 00:25:10.387
- I'd say she's doing pretty good.
- Thanks.

293
00:25:14.985 --> 00:25:16.225
You know, it wasn't so long ago

294
00:25:16.278 --> 00:25:18.144
we were throwing parties like this.

295
00:25:18.239 --> 00:25:20.777
Now we're the only ones left.

296
00:25:20.866 --> 00:25:24.485
Yeah. Last of the first class.

297
00:25:24.578 --> 00:25:26.740
I've been thinking.

298
00:25:26.831 --> 00:25:31.120
Maybe it's time for us to...
move on.

299
00:25:31.210 --> 00:25:33.293
What do you...
Move on where?

300
00:25:33.379 --> 00:25:36.622
I don't know.
It's just Charles.

301
00:25:36.715 --> 00:25:39.048
Whatever is going on between
you two, it will blow over.

302
00:25:39.135 --> 00:25:41.172
No, it won't.

303
00:25:41.262 --> 00:25:43.549
I love him,
but he's different.

304
00:25:44.473 --> 00:25:47.056
Everything is...
it's different now.

305
00:25:47.143 --> 00:25:48.725
Yeah.

306
00:25:48.811 --> 00:25:51.394
We changed the world
so we could live in it.

307
00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.597
Yeah, but maybe
that's what we should go do.

308
00:25:53.691 --> 00:25:56.149
Yeah, but this is our life.
This is what we wanted.

309
00:25:56.235 --> 00:25:58.147
- Not like this.
- Raven...

310
00:25:58.237 --> 00:26:02.231
It's not our life, Hank.
It's his.

311
00:26:02.324 --> 00:26:05.908
What do you think the "X"
in X-Men stands for?

312
00:26:05.995 --> 00:26:08.783
Charles and his X-Men
are where we turn

313
00:26:08.873 --> 00:26:11.240
when facing our worst fears.

314
00:26:13.502 --> 00:26:15.334
Thank you, Mr. President.

315
00:26:17.298 --> 00:26:18.709
Thank you.

316
00:26:21.468 --> 00:26:23.676
All I've really done
is create a world

317
00:26:23.762 --> 00:26:27.722
in which children
can find peace and pride

318
00:26:27.808 --> 00:26:29.891
in being different.

319
00:26:29.977 --> 00:26:34.062
Now, I know that some of you
choose to call us "superheroes."

320
00:26:34.148 --> 00:26:37.061
I must confess, I don't really
know what that word means,

321
00:26:37.151 --> 00:26:39.379
but it is a damn sight better
than what you used to call us.

322
00:26:45.117 --> 00:26:47.074
- Come dance with me.
- You wanna dance?

323
00:26:47.161 --> 00:26:48.618
Come on, Scott.

324
00:26:49.370 --> 00:26:52.455
Did... Did you hear
what the kids are calling you?

325
00:26:52.541 --> 00:26:54.703
- Do I wanna know?
- Yeah.

326
00:26:54.793 --> 00:26:56.283
Phoenix.

327
00:26:56.378 --> 00:26:59.495
It's cool, right? You know,
a bird that rises from the dead.

328
00:26:59.590 --> 00:27:00.831
Whoa!

329
00:27:03.302 --> 00:27:04.509
Uh...

330
00:27:04.595 --> 00:27:06.315
You okay? Hey, maybe
we should take a break.

331
00:27:07.181 --> 00:27:08.466
- Jean.
- Stop.

332
00:27:13.854 --> 00:27:15.254
Wait, wait, wait.

333
00:27:15.564 --> 00:27:17.351
No, stop, stop, stop, stop.

334
00:27:20.903 --> 00:27:22.019
It's Jean.

335
00:27:26.492 --> 00:27:28.292
Jean. Jean, please.

336
00:27:29.495 --> 00:27:31.110
Stop, stop, stop.

337
00:27:31.205 --> 00:27:32.741
Stop, stop, stop!

338
00:27:41.090 --> 00:27:42.456
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Charles.

339
00:27:47.346 --> 00:27:49.491
I'm terribly sorry, everyone,
but I'm going to have to leave.

340
00:27:49.514 --> 00:27:51.598
Thank you very, very much.

341
00:28:31.557 --> 00:28:32.843
What is it?
What do you see?

342
00:28:32.933 --> 00:28:34.389
Nothing.

343
00:28:34.476 --> 00:28:37.310
Her mutation has grown
too powerful.

344
00:28:37.396 --> 00:28:39.763
For the first time,
I can't penetrate her mind.

345
00:28:39.857 --> 00:28:41.689
So that's what
we're doing down here?

346
00:28:41.775 --> 00:28:44.358
Hank built Cerebro
to amplify my power.

347
00:28:44.445 --> 00:28:47.779
I think that's the only way I'm going
to get inside her head now.

348
00:29:07.718 --> 00:29:09.675
Hank, could you turn it up, please?

349
00:29:11.722 --> 00:29:14.465
A little more. Thank you.

350
00:29:17.227 --> 00:29:18.809
There she is.

351
00:29:28.364 --> 00:29:30.008
<i>- Yes, it is.
- Isn't that yummy?</i>

352
00:29:30.032 --> 00:29:32.991
Is it supposed
to look like this?

353
00:29:33.077 --> 00:29:36.286
The mind of a psychic
is a fragile thing.

354
00:29:36.372 --> 00:29:38.158
It takes only the slightest tap

355
00:29:38.248 --> 00:29:40.035
to tip it in the wrong direction.

356
00:29:40.125 --> 00:29:43.584
I had to make adjustments
to her mind when she was young.

357
00:29:45.129 --> 00:29:47.292
What kind of adjustments?

358
00:29:47.383 --> 00:29:48.874
Scaffolding.

359
00:29:48.966 --> 00:29:52.802
Walls, rather,
to keep out all the trauma.

360
00:29:53.430 --> 00:29:55.547
What did you do
to her, Charles?

361
00:29:56.517 --> 00:29:58.053
I saved her.

362
00:30:00.604 --> 00:30:05.144
I think that whatever happened
in space did something to her.

363
00:30:05.234 --> 00:30:07.396
In the process,
those walls that I erected

364
00:30:07.485 --> 00:30:09.523
are being torn down.

365
00:30:12.616 --> 00:30:13.948
<i>Quiet!</i>

366
00:30:15.953 --> 00:30:17.364
What is that?

367
00:30:17.454 --> 00:30:20.947
That... is what I was trying
to save her from.

368
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:25.414
<i>Table for one.
My usual.</i>

369
00:30:26.171 --> 00:30:27.252
What is that voice?

370
00:30:28.674 --> 00:30:30.415
- No...
- Charles?

371
00:30:32.719 --> 00:30:34.176
Charles?

372
00:30:37.933 --> 00:30:39.174
She's waking up.

373
00:30:43.564 --> 00:30:44.771
<i>Jean?</i>

374
00:30:44.857 --> 00:30:47.395
Jean, don't be afraid.
It's only me.

375
00:30:48.444 --> 00:30:49.651
I want you to remain calm,

376
00:30:49.735 --> 00:30:52.854
<i>and I'd like you to focus
on my voice.</i>

377
00:30:54.616 --> 00:30:55.902
Get out of my head.

378
00:30:57.077 --> 00:31:01.162
Just stay calm, Jean.

379
00:31:02.416 --> 00:31:04.624
She's fighting me.
I need you to turn it up.

380
00:31:07.379 --> 00:31:09.462
I heard my father.

381
00:31:11.425 --> 00:31:14.168
- He's alive.
- You're just hearing things.

382
00:31:14.261 --> 00:31:16.173
Jean, your mind,
it needs rest.

383
00:31:17.222 --> 00:31:18.554
You're...

384
00:31:18.639 --> 00:31:20.472
You're lying to me.

385
00:31:22.019 --> 00:31:23.385
I can sense it.

386
00:31:25.481 --> 00:31:26.767
Turn it up.

387
00:31:26.857 --> 00:31:29.520
- No, it's too much already.
- Don't do it, Hank.

388
00:31:29.610 --> 00:31:30.920
- Hank.
- No, I won't do it.

389
00:31:32.821 --> 00:31:34.278
For God's sake, Charles!

390
00:31:35.866 --> 00:31:37.653
Get out of my head!

391
00:31:37.743 --> 00:31:39.029
Charles!

392
00:31:39.119 --> 00:31:40.405
- Charles!
- Charles!

393
00:31:43.373 --> 00:31:44.989
Jean! Are you...

394
00:31:45.083 --> 00:31:47.120
Are you okay?

395
00:31:47.211 --> 00:31:49.418
What happened?
We were outside, and then...

396
00:31:49.504 --> 00:31:51.588
You had an accident.
You blacked out.

397
00:31:54.593 --> 00:31:56.960
Did I...
Did I do... do that?

398
00:31:57.679 --> 00:31:59.011
It's fine.

399
00:32:00.557 --> 00:32:03.264
- No, it's not fine.
- It was an accident.

400
00:32:03.352 --> 00:32:05.192
I don't know
what's happening to me.

401
00:32:05.229 --> 00:32:07.516
I can't control it.
I can't stay here, Scott.

402
00:32:07.606 --> 00:32:08.687
I really, I need to go.

403
00:32:08.774 --> 00:32:09.876
What are you talking about?
Where are you going?

404
00:32:09.900 --> 00:32:12.017
I need to see...
I need to see my father.

405
00:32:14.446 --> 00:32:17.780
- Your fa... Your father's...
- He's alive. I can hear him.

406
00:32:17.866 --> 00:32:19.528
He died in the crash,
remember?

407
00:32:19.618 --> 00:32:21.359
I'm sorry, Scott.
I need to go.

408
00:32:21.453 --> 00:32:23.139
- Hang on, hang on, hang on.
- God, please let me go.

409
00:32:23.163 --> 00:32:24.529
- Please.
- Slow down, please.

410
00:32:24.623 --> 00:32:27.831
I can't control it when it comes.
I can't stop it.

411
00:32:27.918 --> 00:32:29.705
Okay? I could hurt you again.

412
00:32:29.795 --> 00:32:31.706
I'll take that chance.

413
00:32:36.510 --> 00:32:37.626
I know.

414
00:32:39.888 --> 00:32:41.174
I know.

415
00:32:42.014 --> 00:32:43.722
But I won't.

416
00:32:54.360 --> 00:32:56.256
- Is he gonna be all right?
- I'm gonna be fine.

417
00:32:56.280 --> 00:32:58.174
- No, he's not fine.
- I'm going to be fine.

418
00:32:58.198 --> 00:32:59.530
What did you see?

419
00:33:02.411 --> 00:33:04.744
She's all desire.

420
00:33:05.455 --> 00:33:08.619
All rage, all pain.

421
00:33:11.086 --> 00:33:13.293
And it's all coming out at once.

422
00:33:14.881 --> 00:33:16.463
Something's happening
to her, Raven.

423
00:33:16.550 --> 00:33:18.507
She's changing.

424
00:33:19.553 --> 00:33:20.793
Into what?

425
00:33:22.431 --> 00:33:23.547
I don't know.

426
00:33:25.851 --> 00:33:27.183
Jean's gone. She left.

427
00:33:27.269 --> 00:33:29.101
- Gone where?
- I don't know.

428
00:33:29.187 --> 00:33:30.748
Charles, you can track her
with your mind.

429
00:33:30.772 --> 00:33:33.014
Not anymore.

430
00:33:33.108 --> 00:33:34.770
She's grown too powerful,
even for me.

431
00:33:34.860 --> 00:33:36.772
She said she was going
to see her father.

432
00:33:37.904 --> 00:33:39.896
That doesn't make
any sense, right?

433
00:33:41.199 --> 00:33:43.862
Prepare the jet.
We're going to bring her home.

434
00:33:43.952 --> 00:33:46.194
"We"? Charles,
you're in no condition.

435
00:33:46.288 --> 00:33:48.870
I have to stop this.
She's going to find...

436
00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:52.117
She's going to find
nothing good there.

437
00:34:05.349 --> 00:34:09.719
So this is all that's left
of the D'Bari Empire?

438
00:34:13.774 --> 00:34:14.774
Greetings, Vuk.

439
00:34:16.234 --> 00:34:18.100
Have you learned their language?

440
00:34:18.236 --> 00:34:19.522
With ease.

441
00:34:19.613 --> 00:34:21.400
What have you learned?

442
00:34:21.490 --> 00:34:25.200
The power is being contained
inside one of them.

443
00:34:27.162 --> 00:34:30.030
- This primitive species?
- She's stronger.

444
00:34:30.916 --> 00:34:32.282
A mutant.

445
00:34:33.210 --> 00:34:34.792
She has no idea
what's happening to her.

446
00:34:36.088 --> 00:34:38.080
I can use that.

447
00:34:38.173 --> 00:34:40.210
If we can control that power...

448
00:34:41.051 --> 00:34:42.883
we can resurrect our race.

449
00:34:42.969 --> 00:34:44.505
Begin again.

450
00:34:46.932 --> 00:34:48.218
Here.

451
00:34:51.103 --> 00:34:52.469
Where is she?

452
00:35:26.221 --> 00:35:28.008
Can I help you?

453
00:35:30.225 --> 00:35:31.306
Dad?

454
00:35:43.655 --> 00:35:45.772
Jean.

455
00:35:53.039 --> 00:35:55.201
How do you know
where we're going, Charles?

456
00:35:56.334 --> 00:35:58.187
If you can't track her,
how do you know where she is?

457
00:35:58.211 --> 00:35:59.952
You know how.

458
00:36:01.298 --> 00:36:02.789
Jesus Christ.

459
00:36:05.260 --> 00:36:06.501
What did you do?

460
00:36:07.679 --> 00:36:09.466
I protected her.

461
00:36:11.475 --> 00:36:13.467
From the truth.

462
00:36:17.230 --> 00:36:19.438
There's another word for that.

463
00:36:22.903 --> 00:36:24.644
He told me you were dead.

464
00:36:25.864 --> 00:36:28.402
I never thought
I'd be back here.

465
00:36:29.117 --> 00:36:30.653
It's the same.

466
00:36:33.580 --> 00:36:34.821
All of it.

467
00:36:39.503 --> 00:36:43.588
Can I get you something
to drink or-or eat?

468
00:36:44.633 --> 00:36:45.714
Uh...

469
00:36:45.801 --> 00:36:47.542
No, I'm good. I'm...

470
00:36:48.386 --> 00:36:49.922
I'm really good.

471
00:36:54.351 --> 00:36:56.343
It's so good to see you.

472
00:37:00.732 --> 00:37:03.395
Um, I'll get you
some water, okay?

473
00:37:48.029 --> 00:37:49.691
<i>Quiet.</i>

474
00:37:53.285 --> 00:37:54.526
Jean?

475
00:38:04.212 --> 00:38:06.545
All these photos, none of me.

476
00:38:11.553 --> 00:38:13.385
You never looked for me.

477
00:38:13.471 --> 00:38:15.758
- Jean...
- Why didn't you look for me?

478
00:38:15.849 --> 00:38:17.715
Maybe we should sit down.

479
00:38:17.809 --> 00:38:19.345
No, I don't wanna sit down.

480
00:38:19.436 --> 00:38:21.678
Why didn't you come
looking for me?

481
00:38:22.606 --> 00:38:24.939
And don't try to lie.
I can read your mind.

482
00:38:26.192 --> 00:38:28.309
<i>I can't handle her.</i>

483
00:38:28.403 --> 00:38:31.487
I don't even know what she is.

484
00:38:31.573 --> 00:38:33.155
I do.

485
00:38:34.075 --> 00:38:35.782
Then you'll take her?

486
00:38:37.787 --> 00:38:40.325
You didn't even say goodbye.

487
00:38:40.415 --> 00:38:43.203
I didn't get a chance
to say goodbye to your mother.

488
00:38:43.293 --> 00:38:44.973
I was eight years old.

489
00:38:45.003 --> 00:38:47.461
How could you do that to me?

490
00:38:47.547 --> 00:38:49.584
You wanna come in?

491
00:38:52.302 --> 00:38:54.214
Come all the way in.

492
00:38:54.304 --> 00:38:56.796
Don't forget what you did.

493
00:39:01.978 --> 00:39:03.685
I don't know. It's not me.

494
00:39:07.108 --> 00:39:09.270
Quiet!

495
00:39:13.156 --> 00:39:15.944
No. No.

496
00:39:25.502 --> 00:39:27.414
I'm sorry, Jean...

497
00:39:28.171 --> 00:39:30.333
but my whole world died that day.

498
00:39:32.634 --> 00:39:35.843
And... you went with it.

499
00:39:40.225 --> 00:39:43.764
Jean, don't, please.

500
00:39:43.853 --> 00:39:45.060
Stop that.

501
00:39:45.146 --> 00:39:46.182
Stop it.

502
00:39:46.272 --> 00:39:48.264
It's not me. It's them.

503
00:40:12.257 --> 00:40:14.340
You shouldn't have come here.

504
00:40:15.385 --> 00:40:17.321
Why is that? We've only come
to bring you home, Jean.

505
00:40:17.345 --> 00:40:20.304
I don't have a home.
You made sure of that.

506
00:40:20.390 --> 00:40:22.803
Look, your father couldn't handle you,

507
00:40:22.892 --> 00:40:24.428
and we took you in.

508
00:40:24.519 --> 00:40:26.852
You told me
my father was dead,

509
00:40:26.938 --> 00:40:28.474
and you used me for my powers.

510
00:40:28.565 --> 00:40:31.603
No, that's just not true.
That's not what happened.

511
00:40:31.693 --> 00:40:33.355
Jean, we can help you.

512
00:40:33.445 --> 00:40:35.482
I can help you,
but you have to listen to me.

513
00:40:35.572 --> 00:40:37.188
No. No, I don't.

514
00:40:37.282 --> 00:40:38.773
Scott.

515
00:40:41.661 --> 00:40:43.948
He lied to me, Scott.
About everything.

516
00:40:44.039 --> 00:40:46.359
We'll figure everything out together.
Just come back to me.

517
00:40:46.416 --> 00:40:48.296
Remember, you said
you'd always come back to me.

518
00:40:50.503 --> 00:40:52.335
Come back to me.

519
00:40:58.011 --> 00:40:59.011
Jean.

520
00:41:02.098 --> 00:41:04.932
Stay away from me.
Stay away from me.

521
00:41:05.018 --> 00:41:06.225
Stay away from me!

522
00:41:08.730 --> 00:41:11.473
- Stop her quickly!
- Charles, wait, wait!

523
00:41:23.328 --> 00:41:24.328
Jean, please!

524
00:42:02.492 --> 00:42:04.108
Jean, stop!

525
00:42:04.202 --> 00:42:06.785
- I've got the shot. I'm taking...
- No, you're not.

526
00:42:06.871 --> 00:42:09.409
I'm sorry, Hank.
I want Raven to have a chance.

527
00:42:14.671 --> 00:42:16.503
I told you to stay away.

528
00:42:16.589 --> 00:42:18.251
That's never gonna happen.

529
00:42:21.177 --> 00:42:23.009
Please. Stop.

530
00:42:23.096 --> 00:42:24.962
Not until I know
you're gonna be okay.

531
00:42:25.056 --> 00:42:28.094
Something's happening to me.

532
00:42:28.226 --> 00:42:30.434
So come home.

533
00:42:30.520 --> 00:42:32.227
Let me take care of you.

534
00:42:32.313 --> 00:42:33.895
No, you can't.

535
00:42:33.982 --> 00:42:35.769
You can't. You don't...

536
00:42:38.444 --> 00:42:41.187
You don't know what it's like.

537
00:42:42.240 --> 00:42:43.447
Then tell me.

538
00:42:44.367 --> 00:42:46.154
When it comes...

539
00:42:48.663 --> 00:42:50.575
people get hurt.

540
00:42:52.167 --> 00:42:53.829
I'm not afraid of you, Jean.

541
00:42:53.918 --> 00:42:54.918
Look at me.

542
00:42:54.961 --> 00:42:56.918
Focus on my voice.

543
00:42:57.005 --> 00:42:59.042
We're going to get
through this together.

544
00:42:59.132 --> 00:43:00.998
I'm not giving up on you, Jean.

545
00:43:01.092 --> 00:43:03.800
This is what family does.
We take care of each other.

546
00:43:04.596 --> 00:43:06.087
You're my family, Jean.

547
00:43:06.181 --> 00:43:07.717
No matter what.

548
00:43:07.807 --> 00:43:08.807
Stop!

549
00:43:51.017 --> 00:43:55.182
- Raven...
- I can't catch my breath.

550
00:43:57.190 --> 00:43:59.182
No.

551
00:44:00.568 --> 00:44:01.900
I love you.

552
00:44:01.986 --> 00:44:03.978
What?

553
00:44:08.076 --> 00:44:10.068
I...

554
00:44:15.291 --> 00:44:16.873
Raven, please.

555
00:44:21.381 --> 00:44:22.622
Raven.

556
00:44:24.175 --> 00:44:26.462
Raven. I love you, Raven.

557
00:44:28.930 --> 00:44:30.046
No.

558
00:44:32.809 --> 00:44:33.890
No.

559
00:45:00.670 --> 00:45:03.037
<i>We are all at war,</i>

560
00:45:03.131 --> 00:45:04.793
<i>at war with ourselves,</i>

561
00:45:06.259 --> 00:45:09.593
<i>and Raven had been waging
that war for most of her life.</i>

562
00:45:10.596 --> 00:45:12.462
<i>I hope now she's found peace.</i>

563
00:45:15.101 --> 00:45:17.593
Raven died doing
what she did best...

564
00:45:18.438 --> 00:45:20.521
helping a friend,

565
00:45:20.606 --> 00:45:22.313
a friend in need.

566
00:45:25.236 --> 00:45:26.772
She is not gone.

567
00:45:28.323 --> 00:45:30.815
She lives on, through me,

568
00:45:31.534 --> 00:45:33.070
through us...

569
00:45:33.828 --> 00:45:36.241
and through the spirit
of the X-Men.

570
00:45:46.174 --> 00:45:47.415
Is it true?

571
00:45:47.508 --> 00:45:49.295
Jean killed her?

572
00:45:58.728 --> 00:46:00.720
She didn't know
what she was doing.

573
00:46:01.647 --> 00:46:03.559
Jean lost control.

574
00:46:04.567 --> 00:46:06.775
But she-she's still Jean.

575
00:46:07.570 --> 00:46:09.607
She's still our friend.

576
00:46:09.697 --> 00:46:12.189
We can still help her.
We can find her.

577
00:46:13.201 --> 00:46:15.033
And bring her home.

578
00:46:17.997 --> 00:46:21.081
That's... That's what
we're gonna do, okay?

579
00:46:32.553 --> 00:46:34.169
It wasn't an accident, Scott.

580
00:46:36.224 --> 00:46:37.760
She killed Raven.

581
00:46:37.850 --> 00:46:40.308
Maybe you can't admit that
to yourself or to them,

582
00:46:41.020 --> 00:46:42.181
but it's the truth.

583
00:46:43.314 --> 00:46:45.931
That was not Jean,
not the Jean I know.

584
00:46:49.779 --> 00:46:52.066
Sometimes you want to believe

585
00:46:52.156 --> 00:46:54.148
people are something
that they are not.

586
00:46:55.827 --> 00:46:58.570
And then, by the time
you realize who they are...

587
00:46:59.789 --> 00:47:01.200
it's too late.

588
00:47:26.190 --> 00:47:30.480
Do you know, this is where
I first met Raven.

589
00:47:35.283 --> 00:47:38.617
She was just
this little girl, and...

590
00:47:38.703 --> 00:47:41.491
she'd broken in,
looking for food.

591
00:47:42.415 --> 00:47:43.656
I said she could stay,

592
00:47:43.749 --> 00:47:46.958
and that she'd never have
to go hungry again.

593
00:47:47.044 --> 00:47:51.334
And then, I think
I promised her a better life.

594
00:47:52.425 --> 00:47:55.213
And then you took it from her.

595
00:47:55.303 --> 00:47:57.920
- I beg your pardon?
- You heard me.

596
00:47:58.014 --> 00:48:00.381
- Hank...
- This is your fault, Charles.

597
00:48:02.310 --> 00:48:04.017
It's your fault she's dead.

598
00:48:04.103 --> 00:48:06.891
- Come on, that's not fair.
- Fair? No, don't talk about fair.

599
00:48:06.981 --> 00:48:08.750
You messed with the mind
of an eight-year-old girl.

600
00:48:08.774 --> 00:48:10.252
You pushed down
all that pain and anger...

601
00:48:10.276 --> 00:48:11.587
- Jean?
- ...where do you think it's gonna go?

602
00:48:11.611 --> 00:48:13.068
I did that to help her.
What I do,

603
00:48:13.154 --> 00:48:14.756
- I do to help all of them.
- Please, come on, please.

604
00:48:14.780 --> 00:48:18.069
- You still can't see what you did wrong?
- It's just...

605
00:48:18.159 --> 00:48:20.697
No, you need to face this, Charles!
You need to face it.

606
00:48:20.786 --> 00:48:22.466
Come on, admit it
to me right now. Come on!

607
00:48:22.497 --> 00:48:23.738
Admit it!

608
00:48:24.624 --> 00:48:27.116
Charles, just admit
you were wrong, please.

609
00:48:32.131 --> 00:48:33.963
You still can't.

610
00:48:36.761 --> 00:48:39.094
I really hope
you feel better, Hank.

611
00:48:39.180 --> 00:48:42.844
I hope that railing on me five minutes
after I put my foster sister in the grave

612
00:48:42.934 --> 00:48:44.411
- has made you feel...
- This isn't about me.

613
00:48:44.435 --> 00:48:46.371
You, know what? I know what
I did wrong, okay, Charles?

614
00:48:46.395 --> 00:48:48.808
She was gonna leave.
Raven was gonna leave,

615
00:48:48.898 --> 00:48:51.311
and I talked her out of it.

616
00:48:53.653 --> 00:48:55.895
She saw what the rest of us didn't.

617
00:48:58.157 --> 00:48:59.157
And what was that?

618
00:48:59.242 --> 00:49:00.574
This whole time,
we've been trying

619
00:49:00.660 --> 00:49:02.140
to protect these kids from the world,

620
00:49:02.203 --> 00:49:04.570
when really, we should've been
protecting them from you.

621
00:49:11.128 --> 00:49:13.962
I don't know
what's happening to me.

622
00:49:17.510 --> 00:49:18.546
Why?

623
00:49:20.930 --> 00:49:23.047
Why did I do that?

624
00:49:51.669 --> 00:49:53.877
- No civilians past this...
- FBI.

625
00:50:01.053 --> 00:50:02.760
Give us the room.

626
00:50:12.315 --> 00:50:14.352
And who are you
supposed to be?

627
00:50:17.111 --> 00:50:20.024
We're the ones who are going
to help you, Mr. Grey.

628
00:50:22.450 --> 00:50:24.863
I didn't know
she was gonna come back.

629
00:50:26.746 --> 00:50:28.533
I'm sorry for all this.

630
00:50:30.041 --> 00:50:31.532
It's okay.

631
00:50:37.173 --> 00:50:40.382
We just wanna get an accurate
picture of who Jean is.

632
00:50:40.468 --> 00:50:42.755
Tell us about when you
gave her to the mutant.

633
00:50:47.183 --> 00:50:48.219
Um...

634
00:50:50.394 --> 00:50:51.680
Maybe, uh...

635
00:50:53.356 --> 00:50:56.724
it might be better
if I talk to a lawyer.

636
00:51:00.655 --> 00:51:02.692
I'm so sorry, Mr. Grey,

637
00:51:02.782 --> 00:51:05.240
but I need to know
everything about her now.

638
00:51:08.162 --> 00:51:11.030
This truly is
an unfortunate development.

639
00:51:11.123 --> 00:51:12.409
Why-Why is that?

640
00:51:13.125 --> 00:51:16.163
Because it's so much easier
to understand your language

641
00:51:16.253 --> 00:51:17.835
when you're not screaming.

642
00:52:05.928 --> 00:52:07.339
Who are you?

643
00:52:08.723 --> 00:52:10.760
What are you doing here?

644
00:52:14.353 --> 00:52:16.436
Answer the question.

645
00:52:27.908 --> 00:52:29.490
Leave her.

646
00:52:31.620 --> 00:52:32.736
Why are you here?

647
00:52:43.048 --> 00:52:44.505
Are you hurt?

648
00:52:45.468 --> 00:52:46.468
No.

649
00:52:47.928 --> 00:52:49.794
You'll have to forgive them.

650
00:52:49.889 --> 00:52:52.472
They're not accustomed
to uninvited guests.

651
00:52:54.435 --> 00:52:55.471
Please.

652
00:53:06.238 --> 00:53:07.695
Why don't you start
at the beginning?

653
00:53:11.827 --> 00:53:13.443
Whose blood is that?

654
00:53:16.165 --> 00:53:18.202
- What?
- On your shirt.

655
00:53:18.292 --> 00:53:19.328
Whose blood is it?

656
00:53:21.170 --> 00:53:23.787
Look, I'm not Charles.

657
00:53:25.216 --> 00:53:26.878
I can't read your mind.

658
00:53:33.098 --> 00:53:34.714
You hurt people.

659
00:53:36.393 --> 00:53:38.134
- It's been a while.
- But you did.

660
00:53:39.396 --> 00:53:42.355
Yes. What did you
come here to ask me?

661
00:53:42.441 --> 00:53:44.979
How did you stop?

662
00:53:52.034 --> 00:53:54.367
I've lived with vengeance
my whole life.

663
00:53:55.871 --> 00:53:58.238
Ever since I was a child, I...

664
00:53:58.916 --> 00:54:01.829
lost everyone I ever loved, so...

665
00:54:02.628 --> 00:54:04.210
I hurt people.

666
00:54:04.296 --> 00:54:06.333
Yes, killed people.

667
00:54:08.509 --> 00:54:11.217
Killed whatever I thought
would make the pain go away.

668
00:54:14.181 --> 00:54:15.342
It didn't,

669
00:54:15.432 --> 00:54:17.674
no matter how many souls
I sent under...

670
00:54:20.688 --> 00:54:22.395
so I stopped.

671
00:54:23.399 --> 00:54:25.356
I don't know how to stop.

672
00:54:28.320 --> 00:54:30.277
I don't know
what's happening to me.

673
00:54:37.037 --> 00:54:39.120
When I lose control...

674
00:54:41.792 --> 00:54:44.250
things happen, bad things...

675
00:54:47.047 --> 00:54:48.709
to people I love.

676
00:54:55.639 --> 00:54:56.971
Whose blood is that?

677
00:54:59.143 --> 00:55:01.180
Isn't that why you came here?

678
00:55:01.270 --> 00:55:03.387
- What do you think I can do for you?
- I don't know!

679
00:55:03.480 --> 00:55:05.597
Yes, you do.
Whose blood is that?

680
00:55:05.691 --> 00:55:07.460
- I don't wanna talk about it.
- Did you hurt someone?

681
00:55:07.484 --> 00:55:09.129
- Please, I...
- Answer the question, Jean.

682
00:55:09.153 --> 00:55:10.985
- Stop, Erik, you're making me angry.
- Good!

683
00:55:11.071 --> 00:55:12.562
I want you to be angry.

684
00:55:12.656 --> 00:55:14.593
- Show me what happens, Jean.
- I don't wanna hurt you!

685
00:55:14.617 --> 00:55:16.094
What happens when you're angry?
Show me.

686
00:55:16.118 --> 00:55:17.700
- Show me what...
- Stop!

687
00:55:18.787 --> 00:55:20.449
We've got military.

688
00:55:20.539 --> 00:55:21.746
Inbound.

689
00:55:22.917 --> 00:55:24.158
Stay here.

690
00:55:31.091 --> 00:55:32.878
Two birds. US.

691
00:55:32.968 --> 00:55:35.301
Tell everyone to stay calm,
but ready.

692
00:56:05.876 --> 00:56:07.356
All right, that's far enough.

693
00:56:16.345 --> 00:56:18.302
We have a legal right
to be here.

694
00:56:19.807 --> 00:56:21.799
This land was given to us
by the US government.

695
00:56:21.892 --> 00:56:23.804
We have no intention of taking it back.

696
00:56:24.687 --> 00:56:26.053
We're not here for you.

697
00:56:26.146 --> 00:56:28.638
We're looking for one
of the X-Men. Jean Grey.

698
00:56:28.732 --> 00:56:30.849
I haven't seen her
in a long time.

699
00:56:30.943 --> 00:56:32.671
Then you won't mind
if we look around.

700
00:56:32.695 --> 00:56:35.403
<i>I don't have a home.
You made sure of that.</i>

701
00:56:35.489 --> 00:56:36.675
Would you mind
if I came to your home...

702
00:56:36.699 --> 00:56:37.801
<i>This is what family does.</i>

703
00:56:37.825 --> 00:56:40.112
...unannounced and uninvited?

704
00:56:40.202 --> 00:56:41.568
<i>You're my family, Jean.</i>

705
00:56:42.454 --> 00:56:43.820
Look...

706
00:56:43.914 --> 00:56:45.530
I know who you are.

707
00:56:46.458 --> 00:56:48.700
- I don't wanna fight.
- No, you don't.

708
00:56:49.336 --> 00:56:50.872
Then step aside.

709
00:56:51.547 --> 00:56:54.631
We have the same rights
as you and your family.

710
00:56:54.717 --> 00:56:57.551
And like I said,
we're not here for you.

711
00:56:58.846 --> 00:57:01.088
We're here for a girl
who gave up those rights

712
00:57:01.181 --> 00:57:03.798
when she attacked
a squad of police officers.

713
00:57:04.727 --> 00:57:06.593
They have families, too.

714
00:57:07.813 --> 00:57:10.021
Guess you didn't hear
about that.

715
00:57:11.775 --> 00:57:14.267
We don't get the news out here, Captain.

716
00:57:20.492 --> 00:57:22.028
Stop that.

717
00:57:22.119 --> 00:57:23.860
I said stop that right now!

718
00:57:23.954 --> 00:57:26.571
- It's not me.
- It's me.

719
00:57:28.500 --> 00:57:29.540
Jean?

720
00:57:32.629 --> 00:57:33.629
Jean!

721
00:57:36.050 --> 00:57:37.257
Get down!

722
00:58:19.843 --> 00:58:22.051
Get in the chopper and go!

723
00:58:22.679 --> 00:58:24.261
I can't hold it!

724
00:58:25.265 --> 00:58:26.972
Fall back! Fall back!

725
00:58:27.518 --> 00:58:28.678
Let's go, move, move!

726
00:58:30.020 --> 00:58:32.763
Let's go!
Hook in! Move it! Come on!

727
00:58:34.024 --> 00:58:35.664
- Let's go, let's go, let's go!
- Come on!

728
00:58:36.360 --> 00:58:37.670
Give me your hand.
Help me!

729
00:58:54.753 --> 00:58:55.753
Go!

730
00:58:58.173 --> 00:59:00.165
- Leave this place!
- I need your help.

731
00:59:00.259 --> 00:59:02.091
I thought you
protected mutants here.

732
00:59:02.177 --> 00:59:05.261
I am protecting them...
from you.

733
00:59:06.974 --> 00:59:08.465
You need to leave.

734
00:59:09.351 --> 00:59:10.512
Go!

735
00:59:27.828 --> 00:59:30.390
<i>Word coming late tonight
that Congress is considering</i>

736
00:59:30.414 --> 00:59:32.576
<i>temporary mutant internment facilities</i>

737
00:59:32.666 --> 00:59:34.658
<i>for those whose powers
have been deemed</i>

738
00:59:34.751 --> 00:59:37.243
<i>a clear and present danger
to human citizens.</i>

739
00:59:37.337 --> 00:59:40.250
<i>This coming on the heels
of the Jean Grey incidents</i>

740
00:59:40.340 --> 00:59:42.502
<i>which, after destroying
two communities,</i>

741
00:59:42.593 --> 00:59:44.926
<i>and attacking police
and military personnel...</i>

742
01:00:00.235 --> 01:00:01.396
This is Charles Xavier.

743
01:00:01.486 --> 01:00:03.728
I'd like to talk
to the president.

744
01:00:03.822 --> 01:00:06.986
<i>Mr. Xavier, this phone
will no longer be operational.</i>

745
01:00:08.118 --> 01:00:10.826
I have to tell him not to do this.

746
01:00:10.913 --> 01:00:13.747
There's no need to throw away
everything that we've accomplished.

747
01:00:13.832 --> 01:00:16.415
You have to give us a chance and...

748
01:00:26.386 --> 01:00:28.548
<i>If you break something, anything,</i>

749
01:00:28.639 --> 01:00:29.925
<i>I can fix it.</i>

750
01:00:30.015 --> 01:00:31.551
Not anything.

751
01:00:34.937 --> 01:00:37.771
<i>An international search
is underway for Grey.</i>

752
01:00:37.856 --> 01:00:40.599
<i>Authorities are urging citizens
to keep their distance.</i>

753
01:00:40.692 --> 01:00:42.149
<i>Any sighting
should be reported</i>

754
01:00:42.236 --> 01:00:43.727
<i>to the police immediately.</i>

755
01:00:43.820 --> 01:00:45.277
<i>Government officials have...</i>

756
01:00:45.364 --> 01:00:46.855
<i>This man was electrocuted...</i>

757
01:00:46.949 --> 01:00:49.362
<i>Is that all you got?</i>

758
01:00:51.536 --> 01:00:52.993
Give me another.

759
01:01:15.310 --> 01:01:16.596
Hello, Jean.

760
01:01:23.986 --> 01:01:26.729
You can't control
my mind like theirs.

761
01:01:27.739 --> 01:01:29.196
I'm not like them.

762
01:01:30.284 --> 01:01:31.650
Same, please.

763
01:01:34.329 --> 01:01:36.070
How did you find me?

764
01:01:37.374 --> 01:01:40.162
Let's just say I have friends
in high places.

765
01:01:42.254 --> 01:01:43.335
Who are you?

766
01:01:44.256 --> 01:01:46.623
The better question is...

767
01:01:46.717 --> 01:01:47.958
who are you?

768
01:01:48.051 --> 01:01:49.462
Are you a scared little girl

769
01:01:49.553 --> 01:01:51.465
who answers
to a man in a chair...

770
01:01:52.806 --> 01:01:55.514
or are you the most powerful
creature on the planet?

771
01:01:59.313 --> 01:02:01.179
I don't know who I am.

772
01:02:01.273 --> 01:02:02.639
Yes, you do.

773
01:02:03.984 --> 01:02:06.192
You're the girl
who everyone abandons.

774
01:02:10.741 --> 01:02:12.653
Maybe they had good reason.

775
01:02:13.577 --> 01:02:15.409
Because of what's inside you?

776
01:02:16.747 --> 01:02:21.993
You're afraid of it because you think
it makes you bad, evil,

777
01:02:22.085 --> 01:02:25.328
all the words you've been taught
to keep you in line.

778
01:02:26.423 --> 01:02:28.790
Words created
a very long time ago

779
01:02:28.884 --> 01:02:30.967
by men with very little minds.

780
01:02:31.053 --> 01:02:34.296
They can't begin to comprehend
what you are.

781
01:02:34.389 --> 01:02:36.221
Even your X-Men.

782
01:02:37.225 --> 01:02:38.966
And you can?

783
01:02:41.188 --> 01:02:42.188
Charles?

784
01:02:44.441 --> 01:02:46.683
Charles? Charles!

785
01:02:46.777 --> 01:02:49.565
- Hey, Hank's not in class.
- What?

786
01:02:49.654 --> 01:02:50.940
Hank's not in class.

787
01:02:52.574 --> 01:02:53.860
Did you check his quarters?

788
01:02:53.950 --> 01:02:56.237
Yeah, he's not there either.

789
01:03:11.802 --> 01:03:13.259
<i>Where are the rest of them?</i>

790
01:03:13.929 --> 01:03:14.965
No, I'm alone.

791
01:03:16.098 --> 01:03:17.805
What, no Charles?

792
01:03:22.062 --> 01:03:23.223
If you're looking for Jean...

793
01:03:24.314 --> 01:03:26.772
- she's gone.
- No, I know that.

794
01:03:26.858 --> 01:03:28.645
Then why are you here, Hank?

795
01:03:29.611 --> 01:03:31.147
You have eyes and ears
around the world

796
01:03:31.238 --> 01:03:33.230
to help you find mutants
for this place.

797
01:03:34.324 --> 01:03:36.190
I want you
to help me find Jean.

798
01:03:36.284 --> 01:03:38.492
I've no reason to find her.

799
01:03:38.578 --> 01:03:40.410
Not for me.

800
01:03:40.497 --> 01:03:42.033
Do it for Raven.

801
01:03:43.208 --> 01:03:44.415
Did she send you?

802
01:03:47.003 --> 01:03:48.460
You don't know?

803
01:03:51.883 --> 01:03:53.374
Know what, Hank?

804
01:03:54.553 --> 01:03:55.919
Raven's dead.

805
01:03:58.223 --> 01:03:59.589
Jean killed her.

806
01:04:21.121 --> 01:04:23.408
I need you
to help me find Jean.

807
01:04:29.546 --> 01:04:31.833
If I find her, I'll kill her.

808
01:04:33.300 --> 01:04:35.007
I know.

809
01:04:52.068 --> 01:04:53.775
They know who I am?

810
01:04:53.862 --> 01:04:54.898
Yes.

811
01:04:56.406 --> 01:04:58.193
And they're not afraid of me?

812
01:05:00.410 --> 01:05:03.494
The only person here
afraid of your power...

813
01:05:04.164 --> 01:05:05.655
is you.

814
01:05:19.429 --> 01:05:26.017
Go, gather the others. If she can't control it,
then we will destroy it.

815
01:05:31.525 --> 01:05:34.484
This is what you wanted to show me?

816
01:05:34.569 --> 01:05:35.901
No.

817
01:05:36.613 --> 01:05:39.105
This is what I want to show you.

818
01:05:57.175 --> 01:05:59.838
What entered you in space
was not a solar flare.

819
01:06:00.887 --> 01:06:02.628
And it was not an accident.

820
01:06:03.431 --> 01:06:05.138
It was drawn to you.

821
01:06:06.851 --> 01:06:08.592
What-What was it?

822
01:06:08.687 --> 01:06:12.055
A pure and unimaginably
powerful cosmic force.

823
01:06:13.108 --> 01:06:15.145
We saw it enter you in space.

824
01:06:16.027 --> 01:06:19.771
We were there, Jean,
following that force.

825
01:06:20.782 --> 01:06:22.273
Why?

826
01:06:22.367 --> 01:06:25.576
Because it's the spark that
gave life to the universe...

827
01:06:25.662 --> 01:06:28.951
and the flame
that consumed my world.

828
01:06:33.420 --> 01:06:35.833
What remains of my people
searched the stars

829
01:06:35.922 --> 01:06:37.788
for that power,
to control it,

830
01:06:37.882 --> 01:06:41.842
but it destroyed everything
it ever came into contact with.

831
01:06:41.928 --> 01:06:43.419
Until you.

832
01:06:45.307 --> 01:06:47.048
Why me?

833
01:06:47.767 --> 01:06:49.975
Because you're stronger
than you know.

834
01:06:51.313 --> 01:06:53.475
Because you're special, Jean.

835
01:06:58.653 --> 01:07:02.693
With my help, you could
control what's inside you.

836
01:07:03.366 --> 01:07:07.451
Harness that power
to create whole new worlds...

837
01:07:08.330 --> 01:07:10.538
turn dust into water...

838
01:07:11.499 --> 01:07:13.456
water into life.

839
01:07:14.836 --> 01:07:18.295
It's your destiny, Jean,
to become something greater...

840
01:07:19.174 --> 01:07:24.010
to evolve into the greatest force
in the galaxy.

841
01:07:37.651 --> 01:07:40.268
I told you they could
never understand you.

842
01:07:42.113 --> 01:07:44.321
And what they don't
understand, they fear.

843
01:07:44.407 --> 01:07:46.364
And what they fear...

844
01:07:46.451 --> 01:07:48.818
They seek to destroy.

845
01:07:53.583 --> 01:07:55.119
Did Raven suffer?

846
01:07:57.003 --> 01:07:58.335
Not for long.

847
01:08:01.800 --> 01:08:04.463
I know we've had our...

848
01:08:05.845 --> 01:08:08.337
differences in the past, but...

849
01:08:08.431 --> 01:08:10.138
We both love Raven.

850
01:08:12.018 --> 01:08:13.018
Yes.

851
01:08:16.231 --> 01:08:17.438
Yes, we did.

852
01:08:18.233 --> 01:08:20.519
There's been a sighting
of the girl.

853
01:08:20.609 --> 01:08:21.609
Where?

854
01:08:21.694 --> 01:08:23.106
New York.

855
01:08:23.196 --> 01:08:25.188
We'll have eyes on the ground
when we get there.

856
01:09:18.835 --> 01:09:20.416
It's time.

857
01:09:26.843 --> 01:09:28.209
We know where Jean is.

858
01:09:28.303 --> 01:09:29.738
I thought you said
you couldn't track her.

859
01:09:29.763 --> 01:09:31.755
It wasn't me who found her.

860
01:09:31.848 --> 01:09:33.259
It was Erik.

861
01:09:33.349 --> 01:09:34.759
Hank's with him.

862
01:09:34.850 --> 01:09:37.138
They're on their way to her,
and they're gonna kill her.

863
01:09:37.228 --> 01:09:39.514
And anyone
who stands in their way.

864
01:09:39.606 --> 01:09:42.518
Kurt, I'd like you to take
Scott and I there, but that's all.

865
01:09:42.608 --> 01:09:44.377
I want you to leave us there
and then come home.

866
01:09:44.402 --> 01:09:45.938
And me?

867
01:09:46.028 --> 01:09:48.112
I'm not talking
to you now as X-Men.

868
01:09:49.157 --> 01:09:51.523
Scott and I will go and fight
for Jean without you.

869
01:09:51.617 --> 01:09:52.903
End of discussion.

870
01:09:52.993 --> 01:09:56.704
Storm, I have lost
so many of the people I love.

871
01:09:57.624 --> 01:09:59.661
I'm not going
to ask you to go.

872
01:09:59.751 --> 01:10:01.036
I am.

873
01:10:03.087 --> 01:10:04.498
We need you.

874
01:10:05.548 --> 01:10:07.130
I need you.

875
01:10:07.217 --> 01:10:08.549
- I've got your back.
- Look...

876
01:10:08.634 --> 01:10:10.501
End of discussion.

877
01:10:16.392 --> 01:10:18.884
Kurt, close your eyes.

878
01:10:19.478 --> 01:10:21.344
I'll show you our destination.

879
01:10:34.326 --> 01:10:35.487
Where are they?

880
01:10:52.344 --> 01:10:53.960
She's in there.

881
01:10:55.682 --> 01:10:57.048
Hello, old friend.

882
01:11:09.946 --> 01:11:12.313
Save the "old friend" shit,
Charles.

883
01:11:12.407 --> 01:11:13.817
And stay out of my way.

884
01:11:13.907 --> 01:11:15.740
I'm sorry for what she did.

885
01:11:16.870 --> 01:11:18.361
But I can't let you
go in there.

886
01:11:18.454 --> 01:11:22.072
You're always sorry, Charles.
And there's always a speech.

887
01:11:23.793 --> 01:11:25.534
But nobody cares anymore.

888
01:11:26.462 --> 01:11:30.331
We do this here, now,
they'll see us as monsters.

889
01:11:30.425 --> 01:11:32.541
Violent freaks,
fighting on the streets of New York.

890
01:11:32.634 --> 01:11:33.634
What did I tell you?

891
01:11:33.719 --> 01:11:35.962
Damn it, man,
your homeland will be gone.

892
01:11:36.054 --> 01:11:38.012
Everything you care about.

893
01:11:38.099 --> 01:11:39.509
Save it.

894
01:11:39.601 --> 01:11:41.684
If you touch her,
I will fucking kill you.

895
01:11:41.768 --> 01:11:44.010
Don't do this, Erik.

896
01:11:44.813 --> 01:11:47.773
Killing Jean
will not bring Raven back.

897
01:11:49.485 --> 01:11:51.226
The girl dies.

898
01:12:28.273 --> 01:12:29.764
Kurt, I need you!

899
01:12:36.157 --> 01:12:37.864
<i>Kurt, get me inside.</i>

900
01:12:40.036 --> 01:12:41.947
You're not the only one
who can control minds.

901
01:12:42.038 --> 01:12:43.074
Kurt!

902
01:13:37.969 --> 01:13:40.757
They're coming to kill you.
You're not gonna let them.

903
01:13:40.847 --> 01:13:42.463
You're gonna fight back.

904
01:13:54.152 --> 01:13:56.108
Feel the power inside you.

905
01:13:56.195 --> 01:13:58.277
The power is you.

906
01:14:30.646 --> 01:14:31.762
Hold them!

907
01:14:45.702 --> 01:14:47.990
I know whose blood that was.

908
01:14:53.001 --> 01:14:54.538
You cast me out.

909
01:14:55.670 --> 01:14:57.333
Now you come here to kill me?

910
01:14:58.132 --> 01:15:00.044
That's right.

911
01:15:19.445 --> 01:15:21.061
And you couldn't even do that.

912
01:15:25.701 --> 01:15:28.317
Let me show you how.

913
01:16:06.534 --> 01:16:08.070
<i>Scott, a little help?</i>

914
01:16:12.123 --> 01:16:13.785
Kurt!

915
01:16:13.875 --> 01:16:15.241
Kurt! Kurt?

916
01:16:15.334 --> 01:16:17.451
- You all right?
- No!

917
01:16:17.545 --> 01:16:20.288
Come here!
Get me in that house now!

918
01:16:24.009 --> 01:16:25.672
Have you come to kill me, too?

919
01:16:25.760 --> 01:16:26.968
Never.

920
01:16:27.471 --> 01:16:28.587
Jean, never!

921
01:16:29.432 --> 01:16:31.549
I failed you.
I know that, but...

922
01:16:32.143 --> 01:16:33.929
this isn't you.

923
01:16:35.313 --> 01:16:36.929
Kurt!

924
01:16:38.608 --> 01:16:41.942
- Jean, please!
- You have no idea who I am.

925
01:16:42.027 --> 01:16:44.236
I've raised you
since you were a little girl.

926
01:16:44.322 --> 01:16:45.358
I think I do.

927
01:16:47.241 --> 01:16:49.779
She's not your little girl anymore.

928
01:16:50.411 --> 01:16:51.411
Who...

929
01:16:54.331 --> 01:16:55.572
What are you?

930
01:16:58.878 --> 01:17:01.871
Jean, please try and remember
what I taught you.

931
01:17:01.964 --> 01:17:03.125
You can control it.

932
01:17:03.215 --> 01:17:06.084
You can do anything
you set your mind to.

933
01:17:06.177 --> 01:17:07.713
So show me.

934
01:17:10.389 --> 01:17:11.755
Walk to me.

935
01:17:15.018 --> 01:17:16.018
You know I can't.

936
01:17:21.317 --> 01:17:22.317
No!

937
01:17:31.451 --> 01:17:32.737
Please, Jean.

938
01:17:41.754 --> 01:17:42.870
Please.

939
01:17:57.812 --> 01:18:01.806
I can't see
in your mind anymore...

940
01:18:02.858 --> 01:18:05.099
but you can see in mine.

941
01:18:07.280 --> 01:18:08.566
So look.

942
01:18:10.241 --> 01:18:11.732
Jean, look.

943
01:18:15.161 --> 01:18:16.889
<i>And what you choose
to do with your gift,</i>

944
01:18:16.914 --> 01:18:19.451
well, that's entirely up to you.

945
01:18:20.960 --> 01:18:22.621
<i>This could be your new home.</i>

946
01:18:23.670 --> 01:18:25.788
We could be your new family.

947
01:18:27.340 --> 01:18:28.340
No!

948
01:18:30.052 --> 01:18:33.090
Because you are not broken.

949
01:18:41.731 --> 01:18:43.438
Then you'll take her?

950
01:18:43.523 --> 01:18:45.106
Yes.

951
01:18:47.277 --> 01:18:48.277
No!

952
01:18:50.781 --> 01:18:53.898
I can help her in ways
that you can't.

953
01:18:54.451 --> 01:18:56.239
She can't be helped.

954
01:18:56.996 --> 01:18:58.487
She's a lost cause.

955
01:19:02.376 --> 01:19:03.833
<i>No, she's not.</i>

956
01:19:03.919 --> 01:19:06.251
As long as there's someone
to care for her, who believes,

957
01:19:06.339 --> 01:19:07.420
then there's still hope.

958
01:19:11.969 --> 01:19:13.960
Then there...

959
01:19:14.054 --> 01:19:15.795
There's still hope.

960
01:19:30.737 --> 01:19:33.526
I knew. I knew
you were still in there.

961
01:19:36.242 --> 01:19:38.405
He just showed you your past.

962
01:19:41.665 --> 01:19:43.576
Follow me...

963
01:19:43.666 --> 01:19:45.784
into your future.

964
01:19:47.838 --> 01:19:48.838
No.

965
01:19:55.137 --> 01:19:56.937
<i>Set weapons to neutralize.</i>

966
01:19:57.389 --> 01:19:59.222
I never asked for this.

967
01:19:59.308 --> 01:20:00.799
Any of it.

968
01:20:01.852 --> 01:20:05.641
I traveled to the stars
for a gift that you don't want.

969
01:20:08.442 --> 01:20:09.773
Then take it.

970
01:20:12.487 --> 01:20:13.568
Please.

971
01:20:13.656 --> 01:20:15.112
Free me.

972
01:20:18.411 --> 01:20:19.652
I'll try.

973
01:21:07.334 --> 01:21:08.791
Stop it.
You're going to kill her.

974
01:21:09.920 --> 01:21:12.503
Your lives mean nothing.

975
01:21:12.590 --> 01:21:16.800
Your world will be ours.

976
01:21:16.885 --> 01:21:18.673
You'd kill us all.

977
01:21:18.762 --> 01:21:20.594
Yes.

978
01:21:21.348 --> 01:21:22.759
Jean, you have to let go.

979
01:21:25.978 --> 01:21:27.264
Jean, let go!

980
01:21:28.438 --> 01:21:30.179
Let go, Jean. Let go!

981
01:21:33.360 --> 01:21:34.601
Let go!

982
01:21:40.992 --> 01:21:42.825
There's one! Get him!

983
01:21:46.040 --> 01:21:47.040
Jean!

984
01:21:54.882 --> 01:21:55.882
Jean.

985
01:21:56.592 --> 01:21:57.673
Jean?

986
01:21:58.219 --> 01:21:59.880
Jean, Jean.

987
01:21:59.969 --> 01:22:02.450
- Charles, what's wrong?
- I don't know. I can't read her mind.

988
01:22:06.227 --> 01:22:07.718
Come on, out!
Take him out!

989
01:22:07.811 --> 01:22:09.973
Come on, out, out!
You guys, come on. Train.

990
01:22:10.063 --> 01:22:11.374
You four with me, let's go!

991
01:22:11.398 --> 01:22:12.501
- Let's go!
- Come on, move!

992
01:22:12.525 --> 01:22:13.982
Come on.
Move, move, move!

993
01:22:24.452 --> 01:22:26.536
- She's alive.
- Scott, you have to get her out.

994
01:22:26.621 --> 01:22:27.907
You have to... No!

995
01:22:34.045 --> 01:22:35.206
We're clear!

996
01:22:57.027 --> 01:22:58.643
Last one.

997
01:23:00.489 --> 01:23:02.329
We need a clean sweep
on the last three blocks.

998
01:23:02.407 --> 01:23:03.648
Let's go!

999
01:23:20.217 --> 01:23:22.004
My kid used to be a fan.

1000
01:23:31.853 --> 01:23:33.344
Raven had the right of it.

1001
01:23:34.063 --> 01:23:36.932
Jean was never the villain.

1002
01:23:39.862 --> 01:23:41.398
I was.

1003
01:23:45.034 --> 01:23:46.866
I should never have lied to her.

1004
01:23:49.330 --> 01:23:50.536
I was wrong.

1005
01:23:53.166 --> 01:23:56.001
But this power...

1006
01:23:57.170 --> 01:23:59.663
inside of her,
I never put that there.

1007
01:23:59.757 --> 01:24:02.715
I would never do anything
intentionally to hurt her.

1008
01:24:02.800 --> 01:24:06.715
That isn't me
and this is not Jean.

1009
01:24:07.556 --> 01:24:09.718
We can still save her.

1010
01:24:09.808 --> 01:24:12.300
She's still Jean inside.

1011
01:24:21.695 --> 01:24:24.108
<i>We're 10 miles out
from Mutant Containment Center.</i>

1012
01:24:24.197 --> 01:24:25.780
<i>Prepare for prisoner transfer.</i>

1013
01:24:35.626 --> 01:24:38.460
What exactly is controlling her?

1014
01:24:38.545 --> 01:24:39.661
I don't know.

1015
01:24:39.755 --> 01:24:42.246
But this woman, this...

1016
01:24:42.340 --> 01:24:43.581
thing...

1017
01:24:43.675 --> 01:24:44.883
has had a taste of that power,

1018
01:24:44.968 --> 01:24:46.196
and she'll be coming back for more.

1019
01:24:46.219 --> 01:24:47.882
She'll be coming
back for Jean.

1020
01:24:47.971 --> 01:24:50.179
Good. Let her.

1021
01:24:50.264 --> 01:24:52.632
She'll kill her to get it.

1022
01:24:52.726 --> 01:24:55.514
But I promise you,
the killing will not end there.

1023
01:24:56.105 --> 01:24:58.142
That's not what Raven
would have wanted.

1024
01:24:58.232 --> 01:25:00.143
You know that.

1025
01:25:00.901 --> 01:25:02.267
You both do.

1026
01:25:21.422 --> 01:25:22.862
<i>Skipper, are you seeing this?</i>

1027
01:25:24.883 --> 01:25:27.876
Alpha One, you have multiple
hostiles onboard.

1028
01:25:27.969 --> 01:25:29.250
<i>They're heading
towards the back.</i>

1029
01:25:29.304 --> 01:25:31.215
- Open four to five.
<i>- Copy that.</i>

1030
01:25:31.306 --> 01:25:32.638
All right, you two,
come with me.

1031
01:25:32.724 --> 01:25:34.842
The rest of you, stay here,
guard the prisoners!

1032
01:25:34.934 --> 01:25:37.348
Don't be fools!
You need our help!

1033
01:25:37.438 --> 01:25:39.224
Lock it down! Now!

1034
01:25:40.983 --> 01:25:42.894
Goddamn muties
come to spring you.

1035
01:25:42.985 --> 01:25:44.521
They're not mutants.

1036
01:25:44.611 --> 01:25:46.005
Free us, you're going
to need our help.

1037
01:25:46.029 --> 01:25:47.736
We're the only chance you have.

1038
01:25:47.822 --> 01:25:49.108
Keep your mouth shut.

1039
01:26:17.268 --> 01:26:19.385
<i>Mayday! Mayday!</i>

1040
01:26:31.241 --> 01:26:33.152
What's the status
on those mutants?

1041
01:26:33.242 --> 01:26:35.610
<i>We're falling back now! They're not...</i>

1042
01:26:36.413 --> 01:26:38.029
What?

1043
01:26:38.581 --> 01:26:40.164
They're not what?

1044
01:26:40.250 --> 01:26:43.038
<i>- They're not mutants!</i>
- They're here for Jean.

1045
01:26:45.130 --> 01:26:46.462
Get ready to open fire!

1046
01:26:46.548 --> 01:26:48.414
Your kid was right about us.

1047
01:26:48.509 --> 01:26:49.715
We could help you!

1048
01:26:59.937 --> 01:27:00.937
Please!

1049
01:27:03.482 --> 01:27:04.848
Fire!

1050
01:27:16.702 --> 01:27:17.702
There's more!

1051
01:27:45.107 --> 01:27:47.894
We only want the girl.
Step aside.

1052
01:27:47.985 --> 01:27:49.021
No!

1053
01:27:50.195 --> 01:27:51.481
What are you doing?

1054
01:27:52.322 --> 01:27:54.438
What Raven would have.

1055
01:28:13.759 --> 01:28:15.217
Scott, get me to Jean!

1056
01:28:55.093 --> 01:28:56.334
Selene!

1057
01:28:59.723 --> 01:29:00.723
Hank!

1058
01:29:02.142 --> 01:29:03.599
Help Storm!

1059
01:29:30.087 --> 01:29:33.420
No, no, no, no, no, please.

1060
01:29:33.507 --> 01:29:35.920
Don't die. No.

1061
01:30:29.646 --> 01:30:31.040
That's it, that's it, that's it.

1062
01:30:32.607 --> 01:30:33.768
Scott, guard the entrance.

1063
01:30:34.901 --> 01:30:36.187
Jean, wake up.

1064
01:30:36.277 --> 01:30:38.269
Jean, wake up.
You have to wake up now.

1065
01:31:54.397 --> 01:31:56.138
Hank!

1066
01:32:51.996 --> 01:32:54.455
I have no desire to fight you.

1067
01:32:55.083 --> 01:32:56.790
I get that a lot.

1068
01:32:57.585 --> 01:32:58.951
You wanted her dead.

1069
01:33:00.505 --> 01:33:02.588
I had a change of heart.

1070
01:33:26.656 --> 01:33:29.693
I was trying to protect you.

1071
01:33:29.784 --> 01:33:33.277
I was trying to keep
the pain away, but...

1072
01:33:33.371 --> 01:33:35.077
<i>You just buried it.</i>

1073
01:33:36.833 --> 01:33:38.119
Jean.

1074
01:33:41.338 --> 01:33:42.454
Where...?

1075
01:33:44.925 --> 01:33:46.632
Are we inside my mind?

1076
01:33:48.219 --> 01:33:50.085
It's more peaceful than mine.

1077
01:33:54.309 --> 01:33:56.767
I'm so sorry
for what I did to you.

1078
01:33:57.478 --> 01:33:58.719
I know.

1079
01:33:58.813 --> 01:34:01.772
All I ever wanted
was to protect you

1080
01:34:01.858 --> 01:34:03.690
and give you
what you deserved.

1081
01:34:03.777 --> 01:34:06.063
What every child deserves.

1082
01:34:22.837 --> 01:34:24.794
A family.

1083
01:34:25.799 --> 01:34:26.799
Yeah.

1084
01:34:30.303 --> 01:34:32.340
I know you did what you did
out of love.

1085
01:34:33.098 --> 01:34:34.804
I forgive you.

1086
01:34:54.786 --> 01:34:56.902
I know what I need to do now.

1087
01:34:57.871 --> 01:34:59.454
And what is that?

1088
01:34:59.541 --> 01:35:01.577
<i>Protect my family.</i>

1089
01:35:04.629 --> 01:35:05.745
Jean. Jean.

1090
01:38:29.918 --> 01:38:31.375
You want this power?

1091
01:38:32.545 --> 01:38:34.628
You're gonna get it.

1092
01:38:47.559 --> 01:38:49.222
Aah! Jean!

1093
01:38:57.695 --> 01:39:00.438
You can't control it.

1094
01:39:01.241 --> 01:39:06.737
If you kill me,
you'll kill them all.

1095
01:39:23.638 --> 01:39:26.847
Your emotions make you weak.

1096
01:39:34.148 --> 01:39:35.264
Jean.

1097
01:39:36.276 --> 01:39:38.393
Enough.

1098
01:39:40.612 --> 01:39:41.612
Jean!

1099
01:39:52.541 --> 01:39:53.702
You're wrong.

1100
01:39:55.335 --> 01:39:57.452
My emotions make me strong.

1101
01:40:48.473 --> 01:40:49.714
She's gone.

1102
01:41:00.942 --> 01:41:01.978
She...

1103
01:41:04.864 --> 01:41:06.696
She's free.

1104
01:41:49.617 --> 01:41:52.155
<i>I know who I am now.</i>

1105
01:41:52.245 --> 01:41:56.080
<i>I am not simply
what others want me to be.</i>

1106
01:41:56.165 --> 01:42:00.284
<i>I am not destined
to a fate I can't control.</i>

1107
01:42:00.378 --> 01:42:02.835
<i>I evolved beyond this world.</i>

1108
01:42:04.173 --> 01:42:06.960
<i>This is not the end of me...</i>

1109
01:42:07.050 --> 01:42:08.416
<i>or the X-Men.</i>

1110
01:42:10.763 --> 01:42:12.379
<i>It's a new beginning.</i>

1111
01:42:16.268 --> 01:42:19.012
Hey, slow down. Safety first.

1112
01:43:23.001 --> 01:43:24.994
How's retirement treating you?

1113
01:43:25.670 --> 01:43:27.536
What are you doing here, Erik?

1114
01:43:27.632 --> 01:43:29.624
I came to see an old friend.

1115
01:43:31.344 --> 01:43:32.550
Fancy a game?

1116
01:43:35.473 --> 01:43:37.339
No, not today. Thank you.

1117
01:43:41.228 --> 01:43:44.438
A long time ago,
you saved my life.

1118
01:43:46.858 --> 01:43:49.067
Then you offered me a home.

1119
01:43:50.362 --> 01:43:52.730
I'd like to do the same for you.

1120
01:44:08.589 --> 01:44:10.295
Just one game.

1121
01:44:11.592 --> 01:44:13.083
For old times' sake.

1122
01:44:25.815 --> 01:44:27.522
I'll go easy on you.

1123
01:44:28.942 --> 01:44:30.275
No, you won't.
